    "description": "Manage registered agent factories. A factory is a reusable JavaScript orchestration that coordinates multiple subagents; it may spawn dozens of agents and consume substantial credits. Use one only when the user explicitly requests a factory, or when a skill or slash command instructs you to. Do not infer factory use merely because a task could benefit from parallelism. Use \"guide\" to find the factory documentation, \"list\" to discover registered factories, \"inspect\" to review one, \"runs\" to find prior runs and resumable work, or \"inspect-run\" to read the durable result of a single run by ID without waiting for it to finish. Authoring a new factory is unavailable in this session because no extension host is attached or extensions are not running in \"load_and_augment\" mode; only the operations listed here can be used.",
