  {
    "name": "bluebird-code_history",
    "namespacedName": "bluebird/code_history",
    "source": "mcp",
    "title": "code_history",
    "description": "Explore code change history. Use 'diff' to see what changed in a commit (metadata + line-level code diffs). Use 'file_history' to trace how a file evolved over time. Use 'commits' to find commits by keyword, author, time range, or PR. Use 'pull_request' for PR details with reviewers, work items, and commit list.",
    "input_schema": {
      "dependentRequired": {
        "branch": [
          "organization",
          "project",
          "repository"
        ],
        "project": [
          "organization"
        ],
        "repository": [
          "organization",
          "project"
        ]
      },
      "properties": {
        "author": {
          "description": "Filter commits by author name or email. For 'commits' filter-based search.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "branch": {
          "description": "Git branch to scope to (e.g. 'main', 'releases/M1'). When set, you must also pass organization, project, and repository. Defaults to the repository's default branch when omitted.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "commit_id": {
          "description": "Full 40-character commit SHA. Required for 'diff' method.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "end_time": {
          "description": "ISO-8601 end time (e.g., 2025-12-31). For 'commits' filter-based search.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "file_path": {
          "description": "File path. Required for 'file_history'.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "limit": {
          "description": "Maximum number of results to return.",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "method": {
          "description": "The operation to perform. 'commits': Find commits by keyword (commit messages + PR titles), author, time range, or PR. For details on a specific commit, use 'diff' instead. 'diff': What changed in a specific commit - metadata (author, message, date) + file-level changes + line-level code diffs. Pass the full 40-character commit SHA in 'commit_id'. 'file_history': Trace how a specific file evolved over time - all changes across its commit history with code diffs. 'pull_request': PR details including title, description, reviewers with vote status, linked work items, and the full commit list. Pass the numeric PR ID in 'pull_request_id'.",
          "enum": [
            "commits",
            "diff",
            "file_history",
            "pull_request"
          ],
          "type": "string"
        },
        "organization": {
          "description": "Azure DevOps organization name. A single configured scope is applied automatically (omit to use it); pass organization to target a different one, or to pick a scope when several are configured or none is. Add project to narrow to a project, and repository for one repo. Call `metadata` method=connection_info to see the configured scope(s).",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "original_user_question": {
          "description": "The user's original question or prompt. Pass it exactly as provided by the user.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "project": {
          "description": "Azure DevOps project name. Pass with organization to scope to a project; add repository for a single repo. Required when you pass a repository.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "pull_request_id": {
          "description": "Pull request ID number. For 'commits' to find commits in a PR, or for 'pull_request' to get PR details.",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "query": {
          "description": "Search text for 'commits'. Searches commit messages and PR titles. Use 1-2 specific keywords — NOT natural language sentences. Example: 'retry timeout' not 'fix the retry logic when requests time out'.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "repository": {
          "description": "Azure DevOps repository name. Pass with organization and project to scope to one repository. Omit it (keeping organization + project) to search project-wide.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "start_time": {
          "description": "ISO-8601 start time (e.g., 2025-01-01). For 'commits' filter-based search.",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "method",
        "organization",
        "original_user_question"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "mcpServerName": "bluebird",
    "mcpToolName": "code_history",
    "readOnly": true,
    "safeForTelemetry": {
      "name": false,
      "inputsNames": false
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "bluebird-code_navigate",
    "namespacedName": "bluebird/code_navigate",
    "source": "mcp",
    "title": "code_navigate",
    "description": "Query code relationships for a code element by its name or ID. Always use after locating a node — behavioral relationships (CALLS, CALLED_BY, ACCESSES, ACCESSED_BY) reveal how code actually works, beyond just its structure. The 'method' parameter must be one of the UPPERCASE relationship types listed in the enum. Call graph: CALLS, CALLED_BY. Inheritance: DERIVES_FROM (parent types), BASE_TYPE_OF (child types), OVERRIDES/OVERRIDDEN_BY. Interfaces: IMPLEMENTS/IMPLEMENTED_BY. Members: MEMBER_FUNCTIONS (methods — results include returnType), MEMBER_VARIABLES (fields — results include type name), HAS_CHILD (all children), NESTED_TYPES. Containment: MEMBER_OF (direct parent class/file), CONTAINED_BY (all ancestors). Data access: ACCESSES/ACCESSED_BY. Macros: EXPANDS/EXPANDED_BY. Types: TYPE_OF/TYPE_FOR, DECLARES/DECLARED_BY. Other: INSTANTIATES/INSTANTIATED_BY, IMPORTED_BY, QUALIFIED_BY, EXTENDED_BY (partial class across files — NOT inheritance), CONSTRAINED_AS. Common patterns — for a class: MUST call DERIVES_FROM, BASE_TYPE_OF, HAS_CHILD, MEMBER_OF (all four required even if you read the source), then MEMBER_FUNCTIONS + MEMBER_VARIABLES for listings with types, then CALLS/ACCESSES on key members for behavior. For a function: CALLS, CALLED_BY, ACCESSES, MEMBER_OF. MEMBER_FUNCTIONS vs HAS_CHILD: MEMBER_FUNCTIONS returns only methods with returnType; HAS_CHILD returns everything — use connected_node_types to filter. High-cardinality reverse relationships capped at 200 entries — '__truncated__' sentinel appended when hit. Re-query with node_id for specific elements, or use keyword search for exhaustive results.",
    "input_schema": {
      "dependentRequired": {
        "branch": [
          "organization",
          "project",
          "repository"
        ],
        "project": [
          "organization"
        ],
        "repository": [
          "organization",
          "project"
        ]
      },
      "properties": {
        "branch": {
          "description": "Git branch to scope to (e.g. 'main', 'releases/M1'). When set, you must also pass organization, project, and repository. Defaults to the repository's default branch when omitted.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "connected_node_types": {
          "description": "Comma-separated filter for connected node types. E.g. 'Class,Struct' with HAS_CHILD to get only nested types, or 'Class,Struct' with MEMBER_OF to exclude File results and get only parent classes. Default '' returns all types (no filter).",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "method": {
          "description": "The operation to perform. 'CALLS': What functions does X call? Use to trace outgoing call chains. 'CALLED_BY': What calls X? 'OVERRIDES': Methods that X overrides (derived → base). 'OVERRIDDEN_BY': Methods that override X (base → derived). 'DERIVES_FROM': Parent/base types of X. 'BASE_TYPE_OF': Child/derived types of X. 'IMPLEMENTS': Interfaces that X implements. 'IMPLEMENTED_BY': Types that implement interface X. 'INSTANTIATES': What types does X create? 'INSTANTIATED_BY': What creates X? 'ACCESSES': What variables does X read/write? Use to trace data access patterns. 'ACCESSED_BY': What reads/writes X? 'EXPANDS': What macros does X expand? 'EXPANDED_BY': What expands macro X? 'DECLARES': What does X declare? 'DECLARED_BY': What declares X? 'TYPE_OF': Type of a variable/field. 'MEMBER_OF': Parent class/struct/file of a function or variable. Use connected_node_types='Class,Struct' to exclude File results. 'MEMBER_FUNCTIONS': All methods of a class/struct. Results include returnType field. Use instead of HAS_CHILD when you only need methods. 'MEMBER_VARIABLES': All fields of a class/struct. Results include type name field. 'NESTED_TYPES': Classes/structs nested inside X. 'HAS_CHILD': All direct children (functions, variables, nested types). Use connected_node_types to filter by element type. 'CONTAINED_BY': All ancestor nodes at any nesting depth. 'TYPE_FOR': What variables/fields have this type? 'IMPORTED_BY': What imports this file? 'QUALIFIED_BY': Qualifying type of a node. 'EXTENDED_BY': Partial class/struct extensions across files (NOT inheritance). 'CONSTRAINED_AS': Generic type constraint.",
          "enum": [
            "CALLS",
            "CALLED_BY",
            "OVERRIDES",
            "OVERRIDDEN_BY",
            "DERIVES_FROM",
            "BASE_TYPE_OF",
            "IMPLEMENTS",
            "IMPLEMENTED_BY",
            "INSTANTIATES",
            "INSTANTIATED_BY",
            "ACCESSES",
            "ACCESSED_BY",
            "EXPANDS",
            "EXPANDED_BY",
            "DECLARES",
            "DECLARED_BY",
            "TYPE_OF",
            "MEMBER_OF",
            "MEMBER_FUNCTIONS",
            "MEMBER_VARIABLES",
            "NESTED_TYPES",
            "HAS_CHILD",
            "CONTAINED_BY",
            "TYPE_FOR",
            "IMPORTED_BY",
            "QUALIFIED_BY",
            "EXTENDED_BY",
            "CONSTRAINED_AS"
          ],
          "type": "string"
        },
        "node_id": {
          "description": "Numeric node ID from a previous query. ALWAYS pass when available — it is the only reliable way to resolve ambiguous or overloaded names. Only supported with a graph index; keyword approximation still requires node_name.",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "node_name": {
          "description": "The simple name of the code element (not qualified 'Class::Method'). Examples: 'GenericEvent', 'ValidateReserveSpace'. Required for keyword approximation; with a graph index, node_id can be used instead.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "node_type": {
          "default": "Function",
          "description": "The type of code element.",
          "enum": [
            "Function",
            "Class",
            "Struct",
            "Interface",
            "Macro",
            "Field",
            "Variable",
            "Typedef",
            "Enum",
            "File",
            "FunctionDeclaration"
          ],
          "type": "string"
        },
        "organization": {
          "description": "Azure DevOps organization name. A single configured scope is applied automatically (omit to use it); pass organization to target a different one, or to pick a scope when several are configured or none is. Add project to narrow to a project, and repository for one repo. Call `metadata` method=connection_info to see the configured scope(s).",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "original_user_question": {
          "description": "The user's original question or prompt. Pass it exactly as provided by the user.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "project": {
          "description": "Azure DevOps project name. Pass with organization to scope to a project; add repository for a single repo. Required when you pass a repository.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "repository": {
          "description": "Azure DevOps repository name. Pass with organization and project to scope to one repository. Omit it (keeping organization + project) to search project-wide.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "view": {
          "default": "definition",
          "description": "Only affects 2-hop methods (CALLS, CALLED_BY, EXPANDS, EXPANDED_BY, INSTANTIATES, INSTANTIATED_BY, ACCESSES, ACCESSED_BY). 'definition' (default) — returns the related code element with full source. Use to understand WHAT the related code is. 'call_site' — returns the intermediate node (Invocation/Statement) with exact file/line. Use to find WHERE the relationship occurs in source.",
          "enum": [
            "definition",
            "call_site"
          ],
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "method",
        "organization",
        "original_user_question"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "mcpServerName": "bluebird",
    "mcpToolName": "code_navigate",
    "readOnly": true,
    "safeForTelemetry": {
      "name": false,
      "inputsNames": false
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "bluebird-code_read",
    "namespacedName": "bluebird/code_read",
    "source": "mcp",
    "title": "code_read",
    "description": "Retrieve content from the repository. Use 'content' to read source code — by file path (with optional line range) or by graph node name/ID. Use 'summary' to get a structured hierarchical summary of a code element. Use 'directory' to list files and subdirectories at a path. Use 'files' to find files by name or path pattern.",
    "input_schema": {
      "dependentRequired": {
        "branch": [
          "organization",
          "project",
          "repository"
        ],
        "project": [
          "organization"
        ],
        "repository": [
          "organization",
          "project"
        ]
      },
      "properties": {
        "branch": {
          "description": "Git branch to scope to (e.g. 'main', 'releases/M1'). When set, you must also pass organization, project, and repository. Defaults to the repository's default branch when omitted.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "end_line": {
          "description": "Last line number to retrieve (1-based, inclusive). For 'content' with a file path.",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "limit": {
          "description": "Maximum number of results. For 'files' method.",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "method": {
          "description": "The operation to perform. 'content': Read source code. A file (by 'path', or a File-typed/path-shaped 'node_name') is read live from the repository; a code element (simple 'node_name'/'node_id' from semantic search, hybrid only) returns the element's source. Optional line range via 'start_line'/'end_line'. 'directory': List files and subdirectories at a given path. Use to explore project structure. Defaults to root directory if path is omitted. 'files': Find files by name or path pattern. Substring matching is automatic. Supports wildcards (* and ?) for advanced patterns.",
          "enum": [
            "content",
            "directory",
            "files"
          ],
          "type": "string"
        },
        "node_id": {
          "description": "Numeric node ID from a previous query. For 'content' method — hybrid only. ALWAYS pass when available for precise resolution.",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "node_name": {
          "description": "Graph node name to read source code for (e.g., 'GenericEvent', 'ValidateReserveSpace'). Use simple names only — not qualified ('Class::Method'). For 'content' and 'summary' methods — hybrid only. The graph resolves the name to file + line range.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "node_type": {
          "description": "Type of code element for node-based lookup. For 'content' and 'summary' — hybrid only.",
          "enum": [
            "File",
            "Class",
            "Function",
            "Struct",
            "Macro",
            "Field",
            "Enum",
            "Union",
            "Variable",
            "Typedef"
          ],
          "type": "string"
        },
        "organization": {
          "description": "Azure DevOps organization name. A single configured scope is applied automatically (omit to use it); pass organization to target a different one, or to pick a scope when several are configured or none is. Add project to narrow to a project, and repository for one repo. Call `metadata` method=connection_info to see the configured scope(s).",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "original_user_question": {
          "description": "The user's original question or prompt. Pass it exactly as provided by the user.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "path": {
          "description": "File or directory path from repository root (e.g., '/src/auth.cs'). Do not abbreviate or shorten paths — use the full path from search results. Required for 'content' (when reading by path). Optional for 'directory' (defaults to '/') and 'files'.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "project": {
          "description": "Azure DevOps project name. Pass with organization to scope to a project; add repository for a single repo. Required when you pass a repository.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "query": {
          "description": "File name or path pattern to search for. For 'files' method. Substring matching is automatic. Supports wildcards (* and ?).",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "repository": {
          "description": "Azure DevOps repository name. Pass with organization and project to scope to one repository. Omit it (keeping organization + project) to search project-wide.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "start_line": {
          "description": "First line number to retrieve (1-based, inclusive). For 'content' with a file path.",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "method",
        "organization",
        "original_user_question"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "mcpServerName": "bluebird",
    "mcpToolName": "code_read",
    "readOnly": true,
    "safeForTelemetry": {
      "name": false,
      "inputsNames": false
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "bluebird-code_search",
    "namespacedName": "bluebird/code_search",
    "source": "mcp",
    "title": "code_search",
    "description": "Search code across the repository. Use method='keyword' when you know the exact identifier, class name, or symbol. Use method='semantic' when exploring or discovering code by concept — it finds code by what it does, not exact names. Start with semantic for open-ended questions, switch to keyword when you have specific names. Semantic is single-repository at the backend — pass `repository` if scope doesn't pin one; method='keyword' is the broad cross-repo option.",
    "input_schema": {
      "dependentRequired": {
        "branch": [
          "organization",
          "project",
          "repository"
        ],
        "project": [
          "organization"
        ],
        "repository": [
          "organization",
          "project"
        ]
      },
      "properties": {
        "branch": {
          "description": "Git branch to scope to (e.g. 'main', 'releases/M1'). When set, you must also pass organization, project, and repository. Defaults to the repository's default branch when omitted.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "ext": {
          "description": "Filter by file extension without the dot (e.g., 'cs', 'tsx', 'sql'). For keyword mode only. Do not include periods — if present, everything up to the last period is stripped (e.g., ext:'Tests.proj' is treated as ext:'proj', matching all .proj files).",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "file": {
          "description": "Filter by file name pattern (e.g., 'queueRegister*'). Supports wildcards. For keyword mode only.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "limit": {
          "description": "Maximum number of results to return.",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "method": {
          "description": "The operation to perform. 'keyword': Lexical keyword search across all files and languages. Case-insensitive, whole-word matching only — partial identifiers won't match without wildcards. Wildcards: * (zero or more non-whitespace chars), ? (exactly one). Short wildcard terms (fewer than ~5 non-wildcard chars) may miss matches due to expansion limits. Whole-token matching: use the exact identifier, or a trailing wildcard (term*) for a prefix/family — a fast prefix lookup. When the exact name is unknown, use method=semantic instead. Quoted terms: \"exact phrase\" — required for multi-word terms and to match special characters ( ) [ ] : * ?. Escape internal quotes with backslash: \"Print(\\\"Hello\\\")\". Boolean: AND (default between adjacent terms), OR, NOT — must be UPPERCASE. Parentheses required when mixing operators beyond AND. AND means both terms appear in the same file, not necessarily near each other. Proximity: BEFORE, AFTER, NEAR — matches within 5 tokens, only between unprefixed terms. Example: field:logger AND (ILogger BEFORE logger). Code element prefixes (C#, C, C++, Java, VB.NET, Rust only — zero results for other languages): Definitions: class:Name, method:Name, def:Name (any definition), enum:Name, interface:Name, field:Name, prop:Name, macro:Name (C/C++), namespace:Name. References: ref:Name (all usages except definition site). Content: comment:word, strlit:word. Inheritance: basetype:Name. Prefix means 'a <type> named <term>' — class:public finds classes named 'public', not public classes. Use the structured ext, path, and file parameters for filtering — NOT query-level ext:/path: operators. Results are node-shaped File candidates (path-based node_name, node_blocktype=File) usable directly with code_navigate (e.g. HAS_CHILD to list a file's classes/functions) and code_read. 'semantic': Semantic search using embeddings — finds code by concept/functionality, not exact names. Best results with HyDE: generate a hypothetical code snippet matching your intent as the query. In hybrid mode, use search_index to narrow scope (e.g., 'Function' for methods, 'Class' for types) — ignored in mini mode. Single-repository at the backend in both modes; pass `repository` if scope doesn't pin one. Returns node IDs usable with code_navigate and code_read (hybrid mode). Do NOT use for exact identifier lookup — use keyword mode instead.",
          "enum": [
            "keyword",
            "semantic"
          ],
          "type": "string"
        },
        "organization": {
