    "source": "mcp",
    "title": "get_node_tree",
    "description": "Browse the ServiceTree hierarchy one level at a time.\n\nHierarchy: Division → Organization → ServiceGroup → TeamGroup → Service\n\nEach call returns direct children of the given node. Call repeatedly to drill deeper.\nOmit nodeId to get root divisions.\n\nWhen to use:\n- Discover services within an org/team group.\n- Browse hierarchy when service name is unknown.\n\n**IMPORTANT - ID Type Warning:**\nServiceTree IDs (used by this tool) are DIFFERENT from Metadata node GUIDs.\nDo NOT use ServiceTree IDs from this tool as scope.ancestorId or scope.nodeId in search.\nThose search parameters expect Metadata node GUIDs, not ServiceTree IDs.\n\nFor content discovery, use search with scope.serviceIds (Service-level only):\n  search({ query: \"TSG\", scope: { serviceIds: [serviceId], nodeTypes: [\"TSGs\"] } })",
    "input_schema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "nodeId": {
          "description": "ServiceTree GUID to browse. Omit for root divisions.",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "type": "object"
    },
    "mcpServerName": "enghub",
    "mcpToolName": "get_node_tree",
    "safeForTelemetry": {
      "name": false,
      "inputsNames": false
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "enghub-get_service_nodes",
    "namespacedName": "enghub/get_service_nodes",
    "source": "mcp",
    "title": "get_service_nodes",
    "description": "List all content nodes owned by a ServiceTree service, with optional tag filtering.\n\nRequires serviceId (use resolve_service to obtain). Returns content nodes with name, URL, tags.\n\ntags filter — Standard tag values (resolved dynamically from API). Valid inputs include:\n  \"TSGs\", \"Team Docs\", \"Onboarding Guides\", \"OpenAPI\", \"Popular\", \"Featured\"\n  Prefix examples: \"TSG\"→\"TSGs\", \"Onboard\"→\"Onboarding Guides\"\n  Multiple tags use OR semantics.\n\nWhen to use vs search:\n- get_service_nodes: enumerate ALL content for a known service (optionally filtered by tag).\n- search with scope.serviceIds: keyword search within a service's content (pass as array).\n\nWorkflow: resolve_service → get_service_nodes({ serviceId, tags: [\"TSGs\"] })",
    "input_schema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "serviceId": {
          "description": "ServiceTree GUID (from resolve_service).",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "tags": {
          "description": "Filter by Standard tags. Valid inputs include: \"TSGs\", \"Team Docs\", \"Onboarding Guides\", \"OpenAPI\", \"Popular\", \"Featured\". Fuzzy prefix supported.",
