  {
    "name": "icm-search_incidents",
    "namespacedName": "icm/search_incidents",
    "source": "mcp",
    "title": "IncidentAdvancedSearch",
    "description": "Primary tool for finding, listing, looking up, retrieving, or filtering one or many incidents or outages from IcM. Pass ONE object argument named 'incidentAdvancedSearchRequest' with every filter nested inside it (e.g. {\"incidentAdvancedSearchRequest\":{\"severity\":[2],\"owningTeamId\":12345}}); never place filters at the top level. Use whenever the request mentions an incident ID, outage ID, owning team, owning service(s), service category(ies), brand name, assigned engineer (DRI), severity, state, type, environment, tag, keyword, title, or a created/modified date window -- alone or combined. ALWAYS use this tool (instead of any single-id incident lookup tool) when the user provides more than one id. When the user mentions 'outage' / 'outages', prefer the dedicated 'search_outages' tool; use this tool for outages only when full incident detail is required (or when 'search_outages' is unavailable), passing isOutage=true. Intent -> parameter recipes (each goes inside incidentAdvancedSearchRequest): 'show / get / details / info for incident(s) <id...>' -> incidentIds=[id1,id2,...]. 'outage <id>' / 'outages <id> <id>' / 'get outage info for <id> <id>' -> incidentIds=[...] with isOutage=true. 'incidents owned by team <id>' / 'list team <id> incidents' -> owningTeamId=<numericTeamId> (combine with severity / states / dateRange to narrow). 'incidents for service <id>' / 'services <id> <id>' -> owningServiceIds=[<numericServiceId>...]. 'incidents in category <id>' -> serviceCategoryIds=[<numericCategoryId>...]. 'outages for brand <name>' / 'Azure outages' / 'Office incidents' -> brandName=\"<brand>\" (the service resolves brand -> service/category ids and applies brand-route defaults: child incidents and correlated incidents are excluded by default unless includeChildIncidents=true / includeCorrelatedIncidents=true is passed, plus SyntheticTest tag exclusion and TEST environment exclusion). 'incidents assigned to <alias>' -> assignedTo=\"<engineerAlias>\". Severity -> severity=[0,1,2,3,4,25]; state -> states subset of [Active,Mitigating,Mitigated,Resolved,Correlating]; type -> incidentTypes subset of [LiveSite,CustomerReported,Deployment,Unknown]; outage flag -> isOutage. Free text -> keywords; tags (AND) -> tags=[...]; environment in {DOGFOOD,INT,STAGING,TEST,PPE,PROD}; time window -> dateRange.createdAfter / dateRange.createdBefore (ISO-8601 UTC); sort / page -> sortBy=[{field,direction}], top, skip, nextPageToken. Outage-aggregated filters (only meaningful when isOutage=true or combined with a brand-route): 'outages with at least N CritSits' -> minOutageAggregatedCritSitsCount=N. 'outages with N+ support requests' -> minOutageAggregatedSupportRequestsCount=N. 'outages affecting at least N ACE / S500 / QCC / total customers' -> minOutageACECustomersCount / minOutageS500CustomersCount / minOutageQCCCustomersCount / minOutageTotalCustomersCount=N. 'outages with high priority events' -> minOutageHighPriorityEventsCount=N. 'outages with social pickup' -> minOutageSocialPickupCount=N. 'outages impacting N+ regions / clouds / offerings' -> minOutageAggregatedRegionsCount / minOutageCloudsImpactedCount / minOutageCustomerFacingOfferingsCount=N. 'crisis response outages' -> isCrisisResponse=true. 'outages with EIM/SIM engaged' -> hasEimSimEngagement=true (false for none). 'outages with <text> in the outage title' -> outageTitleContains=\"<text>\". Returns a paginated response with items, totalCount, and nextPageToken when more results are available. At least one of incidentIds, owningTeamId, owningServiceIds, serviceCategoryIds, brandName, assignedTo, keywords, tags, dateRange, a severity subset, or a state subset must be provided. NOTE (transition): outage-specific search -- the isOutage flag and the outage-aggregated filters listed above (CritSits, support requests, ACE / S500 / QCC / total customers, high-priority events, social pickup, regions / clouds / offerings, crisis response, EIM/SIM, outage title) -- is moving to the dedicated 'search_outages' tool and will be removed from this tool in a future release. For outage-only queries and outage-aggregated fields, prefer 'search_outages'.",
    "input_schema": {
      "properties": {
        "incidentAdvancedSearchRequest": {
          "description": "The single search request object. Wrap ALL filters inside this object (e.g. {\"severity\":[2],\"owningTeamId\":12345}); do not pass them at the top level.",
          "properties": {
            "assignedTo": {
              "description": "Assigned engineer (DRI) alias.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "brandName": {
              "description": "This is the Organization name like C+E, Office 365 etc for Brand map.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "dateRange": {
              "description": "Optional date/time bounds for created/modified date filtering.",
              "properties": {
                "createdAfter": {
                  "description": "Only include incidents created on or after this time (inclusive).",
                  "format": "date-time",
                  "type": [
                    "string",
                    "null"
                  ]
                },
                "createdBefore": {
                  "description": "Only include incidents created before this time (exclusive).",
                  "format": "date-time",
                  "type": [
                    "string",
                    "null"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "type": [
                "object",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "environment": {
              "description": "The target environment. Must be one of: DOGFOOD, INT, STAGING, TEST, PPE, PROD.",
              "enum": [
                "DOGFOOD",
                "INT",
                "STAGING",
                "TEST",
                "PPE",
                "PROD"
              ],
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "hasEimSimEngagement": {
              "description": "When true, requires at least one EIM/SIM engagement on the outage; when false, requires none (OutageEIMSIMEngagements/any()).",
              "type": [
                "boolean",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "incidentIds": {
              "description": "Incident identifiers to filter by. Accepts a single value or an array of numeric incident IDs. To filter by outage IDs, combine with isOutage=true.",
              "items": {
                "type": "integer"
              },
              "type": [
                "array",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "incidentTypes": {
              "description": "The types of the incident. Accepts a single value or an array; allowed values: Unknown, CustomerReported, Deployment, LiveSite.",
              "items": {
                "description": "Type classification of an incident. Allowed values: Unknown, CustomerReported, Deployment, LiveSite.",
                "enum": [
                  "Unknown",
                  "CustomerReported",
                  "Deployment",
                  "LiveSite"
                ],
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": [
                "array",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "includeChildIncidents": {
              "description": "Include Child Incidents",
              "type": [
                "boolean",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "includeCorrelatedIncidents": {
              "description": "Include Correlated Incidents",
              "type": [
                "boolean",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "isCrisisResponse": {
              "description": "Filter by whether the outage is a crisis response (OutageIsCrisisResponse eq value).",
              "type": [
                "boolean",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "isOutage": {
              "description": "Indicates whether the incident is an outage.",
              "type": [
                "boolean",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "keywords": {
              "description": "Keywords to match in incident title or description.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "minOutageACECustomersCount": {
              "description": "Minimum number of ACE customers impacted by the outage (OutageACECustomersCount ge value).",
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "minOutageAggregatedCritSitsCount": {
              "description": "Minimum number of CritSits linked to the outage (OutageAggregatedCritSitsCount ge value).",
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "minOutageAggregatedRegionsCount": {
              "description": "Minimum number of regions aggregated on the outage (OutageAggregatedRegions/TotalCount ge value).",
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "minOutageAggregatedSupportRequestsCount": {
              "description": "Minimum number of support requests linked to the outage (OutageAggregatedSupportRequestsCount ge value).",
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "minOutageCloudsImpactedCount": {
              "description": "Minimum number of clouds impacted by the outage (OutageCloudsImpacted/Count ge value).",
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "minOutageCustomerFacingOfferingsCount": {
              "description": "Minimum number of customer-facing offerings impacted by the outage (OutageCustomerFacingOfferings/Count ge value).",
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "minOutageHighPriorityEventsCount": {
              "description": "Minimum number of high-priority events linked to the outage (OutageHighPriorityEventsCount ge value).",
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "minOutageQCCCustomersCount": {
              "description": "Minimum number of QCC customers impacted by the outage (OutageQCCCustomersCount ge value).",
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "minOutageS500CustomersCount": {
              "description": "Minimum number of S500 customers impacted by the outage (OutageS500CustomersCount ge value).",
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "minOutageSocialPickupCount": {
              "description": "Minimum number of social media pickups related to the outage (OutageSocialPickupCount ge value).",
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "minOutageTotalCustomersCount": {
              "description": "Minimum total number of customers impacted by the outage (OutageTotalCustomersCount ge value).",
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "nextPageToken": {
              "description": "MCP continuation token for fetching the next page. This is not the partner OData next page token.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "outageTitleContains": {
              "description": "Case-insensitive substring match against the outage-specific title (OutageTitle contains value).",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "owningServiceIds": {
              "description": "Owning service identifiers (list of numeric ids). Accepts a single value or an array. Combined with OR.",
              "items": {
                "type": "integer"
              },
              "type": [
                "array",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "owningTeamId": {
              "description": "Owning team identifier (numeric).",
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "serviceCategoryIds": {
              "description": "Service category ids to filter by (list of numeric ids). Accepts a single value or an array. Combined with OR. Resolved from the brand map when BrandName is supplied.",
              "items": {
                "type": "integer"
              },
              "type": [
                "array",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "severity": {
              "description": "Severities to filter by. Accepts a single value or an array. When null or empty, no severity filter is applied. Allowed values: 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 25.",
              "enum": [
                0,
                1,
                2,
                3,
                4,
                25
              ],
              "items": {
                "type": "integer"
              },
              "type": [
                "array",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "skip": {
              "description": "Number of items to skip (offset) before returning results. Null or 0 means start from the beginning.",
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "sortBy": {
              "description": "Optional ordered list of sort criteria. Accepts a single object or an array. Each entry pairs a sortable field with an ascending or descending direction.",
              "items": {
                "description": "A single sort criterion combining a sortable field with a sort direction.",
                "properties": {
                  "direction": {
                    "description": "Sort direction. Defaults to Descending.",
                    "enum": [
                      "Ascending",
                      "Descending"
                    ],
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "field": {
                    "description": "Field to sort by.",
                    "enum": [
                      "CreatedDate",
                      "LastModifiedDate",
                      "ImpactStartTime",
                      "MitigateTime",
                      "Severity",
                      "Id",
                      "Title",
                      "OutageAggregatedCritSitsCount",
                      "OutageAggregatedSupportRequestsCount",
                      "OutageACECustomersCount",
                      "OutageHighPriorityEventsCount",
                      "OutageS500CustomersCount",
                      "OutageSocialPickupCount",
                      "OutageTotalCustomersCount",
                      "OutageIsCrisisResponse",
                      "OutageQCCCustomersCount",
                      "OutageAggregatedRegionsTotalCount",
                      "OutageCloudsImpactedCount",
                      "OutageCustomerFacingOfferingsCount"
                    ],
                    "type": "string"
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "field"
                ],
                "type": "object"
              },
              "type": [
                "array",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "states": {
              "description": "Incident states to filter by. Accepts a single value or an array. When null or empty, no state filter is applied. Allowed values: Active, Mitigating, Mitigated, Resolved, Correlating.",
              "items": {
                "description": "Lifecycle state of an incident. Allowed values: Active, Mitigating, Mitigated, Resolved, Correlating.",
                "enum": [
                  "Active",
                  "Resolved",
                  "Mitigating",
                  "Mitigated",
                  "Correlating"
                ],
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": [
                "array",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "tags": {
              "description": "Incident tags to filter by. Accepts a single value or an array. All tags must match.",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": [
                "array",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "title": {
              "description": "The title of the incident.",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "top": {
              "description": "Maximum number of items to return. If null, the default is used.",
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null"
              ]
            }
          },
          "type": "object"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "incidentAdvancedSearchRequest"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "mcpServerName": "icm",
    "mcpToolName": "search_incidents",
    "readOnly": true,
    "safeForTelemetry": {
      "name": false,
      "inputsNames": false
    }
  },
